          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} Model structures
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} present
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-presheaves
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localizations of these
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-sheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models+for+%E2%88%9E-stack+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} models for ∞-stack (∞,1)-toposes
          %p Recall that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                is a way to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
                an
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                in the context of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
                on an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                are given by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op} \to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
          %p
            This suggests that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            can be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [C^{op},SSet] \simeq [\Delta^{op}, PSh(C)]
          %p
            – the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaves
            \.
          %p
            Various interrelated flavors of model structures on the category of simplicial presheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            have been introduced and studied since the 1970s, originally by K. Brown and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Andre Joyal
            and then developed in detail by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
          %p
            Notice that when regarded as a presentation of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            – corresponds to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectified+%E2%88%9E-stack"} rectified ∞-stack
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
          %p In
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p
            a fully general definition of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of ∞-stacks
            is given it is shown – proposition 6.5.2.1 – that, indeed, the Brown–Joyal–Jardine model is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of that.
          %p More precisely
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure on simplicial presheaves
                on a category is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
                of the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} Čech model structure on simplicial presheaves
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
                of the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
                of the
                %em hypercompletion
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
                (see the discussion at
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
                of the global
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                structure to the local one presents the corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
                from presheaves to sheaves, mimicking the corresponding statement for a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
          %p
            Originally K. Brown had considered in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} BrownAHT
            not a model structure on simplicial presheaves but
          %ul
            %li
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
              structure on locally Kan simplicial sheaves (see there for details)
          %p and Joyal had originally considered a
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"}> local model structure on simplicial sheaves
              \.
          %p
            Joyal’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} local model structure on simplicial sheaves
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to the injective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %p
            By repackaging
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoids"} simplicial groupoids
            one obtains a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+presheaves+of+simplicial+groupoids"} model structure on presheaves of simplicial groupoids
            which is also Quillen equivalent to the above.
          %p
            If K. Brown’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            on locally Kan simplicial sheaves is restricted to globally Kan simplicial sheaves on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough point
            then it is the full subcategory on the fibrant objects in the projective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} local model structure on simplicial sheaves
          %p
            But since in all cases the weak equivalences are the same (where they apply, for Brown’s model if the topos has enough points), all these local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical categories
            define equivalent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy categories
          %p
            By Lurie’s result these are in each case in turn equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          %p
            Various old results appear in a new light this way. For instance using the old result of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} BrownAHT
            on the way ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            is embedded in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of simplicial sheaves, one sees that the old right derived functor definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            really computes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
            of a sheaf of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold%E2%80%93Kan+correspondence"} Dold–Kan correspondence
            as a simplicial sheaf.
          %h2#the_different_model_structures_and_their_interrelation The different model structures and their interrelation
          %p
            It is the very point of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures on a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            that there may be several of them: each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presenting
            the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            but also each suited for different computational purposes.
          %p So it is good that there are many model structures on simplicial (pre)sheaves, as there are.
          %h3#injectiveprojective__localglobal__presheavessheaves Injective/projective - local/global - presheaves/sheaves
          %p The following diagram is a map for part of the territory:
