          %p Here
          %ul
            %li
              %p “inj” denotes the injective model structure: cofibrations are objectwise cofibrations
            %li
              %p “proj” denotes the projective model structure: fibrations are objectwise fibrations
            %li
              %p no “loc” subscript means global model structure: weak equivalences are the objectwise weak equivalences:
            %li
              %p
                “l loc” denotes
                %strong left
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
                at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
                (at
                = succeed "wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} topos has enough points
          %p
            The identity functor on the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SPSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPSh(C)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            for the projective and injective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure
            and this is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} local model structures on simplicial sheaves
            are just the restrictions of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} those on simplicial presheaves
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JardineLecture"} Jardine
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Blander"} Blander, theorem 2.1, 2.2
          %p
            These are related by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            given by the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            as a full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of that of presheaves – with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            – and this is also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %p
            The characteristic of the
            %em left
            Bousfield localizations is that for them the fibrant objects are those that satisfy
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+for+simplicial+presheaves"} descent for simplicial presheaves
          %p In either case
          %ul
            %li
              the global model structures
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
          %p while
          %ul
            %li
              the local model structures
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              (i.e.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
          %p
