          %h3#reedy_and_intermediate_model_structures Reedy and intermediate model structures
          %p To some extent the injective and projective model structures on simplicial presheaves are the two extremes of a larger family of model structures on simplicial presheaves that all have the same weak equivalences but different classes of cofibrations.
          %p
            Notably if the domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has the special property that it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
            there is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C, sSet]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
            and we have
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          .maruku-equation
