          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This follows using the arguments in the proof of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, 6.5.2.14
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. A.3.7.6
          %h2#FibAndCofibObjects Fibrant and cofibrant objects
          %h3#fibrant_objects Fibrant objects
          %p
            The fibrant objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
            are those that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                are fibrant with respect to the respective
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure
            %li
              %p
                and satisfy
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+for+simplicial+presheaves"} descent for simplicial presheaves
          %p
            This descent condition is the analog in this model of the
            = succeed "-condition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            = succeed "-condition." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
          %p
            Since the fibrancy condition in the global projective model structure is simple – it just requires that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
            is in fact a presheaf of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %p
            On the other hand the cofibrancy condition on objects is entirely
            %em trivial
            in the global and local injective model structure: since a cofibration there is just an objectwise cofibration, and since every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            is cofibrant, every object is injective cofibrant.
          %p
            But the cofibrant objects in the projective structure are not too nasty either: every object that is degreewise a coproduct of representables is cofibrant. In particular the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+cover"} good cover
            (see below for more details) is a projectively cofibrant object.
          %p
            A
            %strong cofibrant replacement
            functor in the local projective structure is discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Dugger01"} Dugger 01
          %p
            Something related to a
            %strong fibrant replacement
            functor (“
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-stackification”) is discussed in section 6.5.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %h3#CofibrantObjects Cofibrant objects
          %p
            In the injective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
            all objects are cofibrant. For the projective local structure
          %p necessary and sufficient conditions are given here:
          %ul
            %li#Garner13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/127187/381"} MO comment
          %p
            More specifically, there is the following useful statement (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projectively+cofibrant+diagram"} projectively cofibrant diagram
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Low"} Low, remark 8.2.3
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A simplicial presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in sPSh(C)
              is said to have
              %strong free degeneracies
              or the
              %strong degenerate cells split off
              if in each degree there is a
              = succeed "-presheaf" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} sub
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi k
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_k \hookrightarrow X_k
              such that the canonical mophism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mo :
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi surj
                          %mo .
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %munder
                            %mrow
                              %mi σ
                              %mo :
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo →
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mrow
                              %mi surj
                              %mo .
                        %msup
                          %mi σ
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\coprod_{\underset{surj.}{\sigma : [k] \to [n]}}
                    N_n \stackrel{\coprod_{\underset{surj.}{\sigma : [k] \to [n]}} \sigma^*}{\to}
                    F_k
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p So if degenerate cells split off we have in particular that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                    %mi nd
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                    %mi dg
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_k = X_k^{nd} \coprod X_k^{dg}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                    %mi nd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k^{nd}
            is the presheaf of non-degenerate
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                    %mi dg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k^{dg}
            is a separate presheaf containing all the degenerate cells (and itself a coproduct over separate presheaves for each degree and order of degeneracy).
          %p
          #DuggerSufficientProjectiveCofibrancyCondition.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              In the
              %em projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure
              all objects that are
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  degreewise
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
              %li
                %p and whose degenerate cells split off
            %p are cofibrant.
            %p
          %p
            This is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Dugger01"} Dugger 01, Cor. 9.4
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong (split hypercovers)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              is an acyclic fibration in the local projective model structure with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a representable and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              cofibration in the above way, it is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+hypercover"} split hypercover
              \.
            %p
              All
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
              coming from an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              have split degeneracies. The condition that the Čech nerve be degreewise a coproduct of representables is a condition akin to that of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %em height
              0.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (good cover)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              with a weak equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPSh(C)^{loc}
              is a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+cover"} good cover
              if it is degreewise a coproduct of
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This reduces to the ordinary notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+cover"} good cover
              as an open cover by contractible spaces such that all finite intersections of these are again contractibe when using a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              like
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
          %h3#CofibrantReplacement Cofibrant replacement
          %p In
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DuggerUniv.pdf", :title => "Universal homotopy theories"} Universal homotopy theories
          %p a useful cofibrant replacement functor for the projective local model structure is discussed.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A  \in PSh(C) \hookrightarrow SPSh(C)
              an ordinary presheaf (simplicially discrete simplicial presheaf) let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde Q A
              be the simplicial presheaf which in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi k
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\tilde Q A)_k := \coprod_{U_k \to U_{k-1} \to \cdots \to U_0 \to A} U_k
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_k
              range over the representables, i.e. the objects in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi SPSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow SPSh(C)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in SPSh(C)
              an arbitrary simplicial presheaf let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q A
              be the diagonal of the bisimplicial presheaf obtained by applying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde Q
              degreewise
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ⋯
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 0
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 0
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Q A =
                    \\left(
                    \\cdots
                    \\coprod_{U_1 \to U_0 \to A_1}
                    U_1
                    \\stackrel{\to}{\to}\coprod_{U_0 \to A_0} U_0
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in SPSh(C)
              the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q A
              is cofibrant and is weakly equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SPSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi proj
                        %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPSh(C)_{proj}^{loc}
          %p This is in prop 2.8 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Universal+Homotopy+Theories"} Universal Homotopy Theories
          %h2#local_fibrations Local fibrations
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+fibration"} local fibration
            or
            %em local weak equivalence
            of simplicial (pre)sheaves is defined to be one whose lifting property is satisfied after refining to some cover.
          %p
            %strong> Warning
            \. Notice that this is a priori unrelated to equivalences and fibrations with respect to any local model structure.
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
            = succeed "wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
          %p
            This is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Jardine96"}> Jardine 96
            ).
          %h2#Descent Localization and descent
          %h3{:id => "ČechLocalization"} Čech localization at Grothendieck (pre)topologies
          %p
            We discuss some aspects of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
            of the projective global model structure on simplicial presheaves at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topologies"} Grothendieck topologies
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            families. By the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+localization"} topological localization
            these are models for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+localization"} topological localization
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-sheaves
          %p
            The central reference is (
            %a{:href => "#DuggerHollanderIsaksen"}> DuggerHollanderIsaksen
            ) with the central theorem being this one:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              given by a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(C)_{proj}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sPSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(C)_{inj}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the set of all
