          %h2#references References
          %p Introductions:
          %ul
            %li#Dugger98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Dugger"}> Dan Dugger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sheaves and homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.uoregon.edu/~ddugger/cech.html"} web
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.uoregon.edu/~ddugger/cech.dvi"} dvi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/cech.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DuggerSheavesAndHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Jardine07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"}> J. F. Jardine
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fields Lectures: Simplicial presheaves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.uwo.ca/faculty/jardine/courses/fields/fields-01.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Jardine-SimplicialPresheaves.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/jardine/courses/fields/fields_lectures.html"} webpage
          %p Detailed discussion of the injective model structures on simplicial presheaves:
          %ul
            %li#JardineLecture
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial presheaves
                %strong 47
                (1987) 35-87 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(87)90100-9"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(87)90100-9
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stacks and the homotopy theory of simplicial sheaves
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.hha/1139840259"} euclid:hha/1139840259
            %li#Jardine96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Boolean localization, in practice
                %strong 1
                (1996), 245-275 (
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-bielefeld.de/documenta/vol-01/13.html"}> documenta:vol-01/13
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Local+homotopy+theory"} Local homotopy theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4939-2300-7"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4939-2300-7
          %p The projective model structure is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Dugger01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Universal homotopy theories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Dugger/dduniv.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0007070"} arXiv:math/0007070
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.2001.2014"} doi:10.1006/aima.2001.2014
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Benjamin Blander,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Local projective model structures on simplicial presheaves
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1023/a:1013302313123"} doi
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-spaces"} derived hom-spaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+complexes"}> function complexes
            ) in the projective model structure on simplicial presheaves:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Function complexes for diagrams of simplicial sets
              %strong 86
              2 (1983) 139-147 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/1385-7258(83)90051-3"}> doi:10.1016/1385-7258(83)90051-3
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/82652265.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A brief review in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Hodge+theory"} nonabelian Hodge theory
            is in section 4 of
          %ul
            %li#Olsson
              Martin Olsson,
              %em
                Towards non-abelian
                = succeed "-adic" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~molsson/PHT3-24-08.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A detailed study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            for simplicial presheaves is given in
          %ul
            %li#DuggerHollanderIsaksen
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sharon+Hollander"} Sharon Hollander
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Isaksen"} Daniel Isaksen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hypercovers and simplicial presheaves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/s0305004103007175"} doi
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0205027"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Isaksen"} Daniel Isaksen
                %em Weak equivalences of simplicial presheaves
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0205025"}> arXiv
                )
          %p A survey of many of the model structures together with a treatment of the left local projective one is in
          %ul
            %li#Blander
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benjamin+Blander"}> Benjamin Blander
              ,
              %em Local projective model structure on simplicial presheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0462/combination2.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Isaksen"}> Daniel Isaksen
              ,
              %em Flasque model structure for simplicial presheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0679/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0679/flasque.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The characterization of the model category of simplicial presheaves as the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the (hypercompletion of) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            on a site is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/highertopoi.pdf#page=528"} proposition 6.5.2.1
                of
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                  ,
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p
            A set of lecture notes on simplicial presheaves with an eye towards algebraic sites and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"}> Bertrand Toen
              ,
              %em Simplicial presheaves and derived algebraic geometry
              , lecture at
              %a{:href => "http://www.crm.es/HigherCategories/"} Simplicial methofs in higher categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.crm.cat/HigherCategories/hc1.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Last not least, it is noteworthy that the idea of localizing simplicial sheaves at stalkwise weak equivalences is already described and applied in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"}> Kenneth Brown
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} Abstract Homotopy Theory and Generalized Sheaf cohomology
              ,
          %p
            using instead of a full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure the more lightweight one of a Brown
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
          %p A comparison between Brown-Gersten and Joyal-Jardine approach:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"}> Vladimir Voevodsky
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory of simplicial presheaves in completely decomposable topologies
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0805.4578"} arxiv/0805.4578
          %p
            The proposal for descent objects for strict
            = succeed "-groupoid-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a{:href => "#DescentForStrictInf"} Descent for strict infinity-groupoids
            appeared in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              %em Categorical and combinatorial aspects of descent theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0303175"}> arXiv
              )
          %p The relation to the general descent conditionF is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"}> Dominic Verity
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verity+on+descent+for+strict+omega-groupoid+valued+presheaves"} Relating descent notions
          %p A useful collection of facts is in
          %ul
            %li#Low
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhen+Lin+Low"}> Zhen Lin Low
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Notes+on+homotopical+algebra"} Notes on homotopical algebra
